# Vox License

Vox is **source-available, not open source.** Its full source is public, and it
is **free for personal and individual use** — including freelancers and
contractors using it for their own paid client work. **Use by a company or
organization (for example, deploying Vox across a team) requires a paid
commercial license.** You may read, modify, and share Vox non-commercially, but
you may not sell it or build a paid product on it.

The legal terms are the **PolyForm Noncommercial License 1.0.0** (reproduced in
full below), together with the **Additional Grant for Individuals** and the
**Commercial License** note that follow it. For commercial or enterprise
licensing, contact **vox@rizenhq.com**.

Required Notice: Copyright 2026 Resonance Logic, LLC (https://rizenhq.com)

